# Decimal division of repeating and exact quotients

Divides 1 by 3 to verify a repeating quotient displays truncated to four
fractional digits while the stored value stays exact, then divides 10 by 4
to verify an exact quotient keeps its own scale. Every divisor carries a
decimal annotation so both cases exercise same-type division.

>>> source
const repeating_dividend: decimal = 1
const repeating_divisor: decimal = 3
const quarters_dividend: decimal = 10
const quarters_divisor: decimal = 4

// Verifies a repeating quotient displays truncated to four fractional digits.
const repeating: decimal = repeating_dividend / repeating_divisor
print(repeating)

// Verifies an exact quotient keeps its scale.
const exact_quarters: decimal = quarters_dividend / quarters_divisor
print(exact_quarters)

<<< stdout
0.3333
2.50

<<< stderr
